## Pros and Cons: Men's Princess Cut Ring

### Pros

- **Princess cut costs 35% less than round at the same carat weight.** A [1ct GIA G-VS2 Ideal princess is $2,212](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28961307?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). The same quality in round starts at $3,230. Same carat, same certification, real savings.
- **Square shape reads as precision on a men's band.** The princess stone aligns with the band geometry. It looks designed, not decorative. That's the visual case for princess on your ring.
- **More stone face-up for less money.** A 1ct princess (5.5mm × 5.5mm) covers 79% of a 7mm band at $2,212. A 1ct round (6.5mm) covers 93% at $3,230. You get more stone surface per dollar with princess.
- **Lab-grown princess reaches D-IF at 1.5ct for $2,980.** The [GCAL 1.76ct E-IF lab princess at $2,980](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29417594?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is a certified, flawless-grade stone. Natural equivalent: $14,000+.
- **Full metal choice across all tiers.** White gold, yellow gold, rose gold, and platinum on every solitaire design. The taste preference does not add to the stone budget.

### Cons

- **V-prong is non-negotiable — and not automatic.** Standard setters default to round-head prongs. You have to ask for V-prong heads. If you don't, the corners are exposed. It's the most common and most expensive mistake in princess solitaire settings.
- **Princess corners chip under daily impact.** Even with V-prongs, princess cut corners are more vulnerable than a round stone's curved girdle. Men's active wear — gym, tools, manual work — creates impact scenarios that round stones handle better. Annual prong inspection is required.
- **Stone replacement, not repair.** A chipped princess corner cannot be re-polished to restore the original shape without significant carat loss. A re-polished 1ct princess might come back as 0.80ct with changed proportions. The industry default is replacement. Budget for it.
- **No channel set princess in certified inventory.** Channel rings in this category use round brilliants. If you want a princess channel band, it requires custom work.
- **18k settings cost $400–$900 more for a softer metal.** The [18k Round Diamond Channel at $2,832](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/mens-round-diamond-channel-engagement-ring-in-18k-white-gold-1-3-ct-tw-item-147395?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is $744 more than the 14k version. 18k is softer. Skip all 18k across this category.

